				<pubDate>Sat, 13 Jun 2020 14:54:35 +0000</pubDate>
								<wikidot:authorUserId>3146689</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>This isn't as scary as it's weird/surreal, with trippy visuals that keep your mind occupied while reading. Not to say that it's bad though, I did enjoy the imagery here a lot, and that feeling of surrealness is the main reason for me to give this a +1.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13408113#post-4685696</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13408113/theosis#post-4685696</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 12 Jun 2020 14:25:30 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>SilentWatcher</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>5399549</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I felt like there was way too much purple prose in this story. I was really engaged and slightly spooked at the beginning, but the mad curiosity that usually pushes you through a horror story just got torn to pieces by the time I finished the section on the hallucinations. In the end, it felt more like some kind of prophetic Christian short story then anything very creepypasta. Downvote for now.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
