ttp://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1956625)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drchandra" >DrChandra</a></span><br /> and especially <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/absentmindednihilist" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2812984&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1591429074" alt="AbsentmindedNihilist" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2812984)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/absentmindednihilist" >AbsentmindedNihilist</a></span> for beta-reading, critiquing, and developing this piece. Enjoy.</p> <p><a href="https://ccsearch.creativecommons.org/photos/c09b9e32-b8de-4767-8d76-5a0793cf69b6">Image Credit I</a><br /> <a href="https://ccsearch.creativecommons.org/photos/1bc9e286-148a-439c-9f5f-d3539fe55ca4">Image Credit II</a></p> <p>Side note: Laures and Senni did not actually suffer from sensory loss in real life. I wouldn't do something as insensitive as tying in an actual tragedy with SCP stuff. The experiment did not result in any negative side effects.</p> 
